POSITIVE CONTROL #1: PASS


Why the agreement is EXACT rather than merely close: k_n = 2^n are exact
powers of two, so multiplying by them only shifts the IEEE754 exponent and
leaves the mantissa untouched. The two implementations associate their
products differently -- (k*a)*a here, k*(a*a) there -- which for a generic
k would differ at ~1e-14, but for a power of two is bit-identical. A shell
model with spacing lambda != 2 would NOT reproduce exactly, and this
control would then need a tolerance rather than an equality.

